WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.234 line:88%
[Upbeat instrumental music]
Want your app to sort messages your way?

00:00:02.354 --> 00:00:05.511 line:88%
Start with examples and the right category for each one.

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:09.893 line:88%
The base model stays fixed.

00:00:10.013 --> 00:00:12.253 line:88%
A small task head learns from your labels.

00:00:12.373 --> 00:00:14.698 line:88%
Here, that improves the task's accuracy.

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:18.021 line:88%
Next, choose an error target.

00:00:18.141 --> 00:00:20.829 line:88%
Separate examples check which answers qualify.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:23.146 line:88%
Those examples never train the task.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.642 line:88%
When an answer qualifies, your app can route it automatically.

00:00:27.762 --> 00:00:31.069 line:88%
Otherwise, keep the prediction as a suggestion for review.

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.981 line:88%
Here, over thirteen hundred messages qualify.

00:00:35.101 --> 00:00:36.274 line:88%
Some are still wrong.

00:00:36.394 --> 00:00:39.210 line:88%
Keep a review path, and watch for changing traffic.
